      "data": {
        "text": "**Considering Database Options**\n\nI'm currently evaluating the best external provider for upserting JSON documents, focusing on document databases. I'm leaning toward either MongoDB Atlas or a similar document database. I'm trying to decide which of these to make identifiable in the generated `upsert_document.py` file.\n\n\n**Defining Upsert Function**\n\nNow, I'm structuring the `upsert_document.py` file. I'm building an `upsert_document` function to handle the upsert logic. This function will take the document, the database name, the collection name, and a primary key field as input. The connection string will be securely read from an environment variable. I'm focusing on incorporating `pymongo` for the MongoDB interaction.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789860678113,
          "start": 1789860673250
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc0276e2001HxJmLur1MsP9m5",
